# The program `takes-a-title`, where `lend` binds the title to a name before it hands it on: `t = self.title;
# other.take(t, None)`. A projection bound to a name first is still the projection (#121, #174): the call is handed the
# first chart and fills `fig` through the field `title`, as `other.take(self.title, None)` does, so `self.fig = fig` in
# `take` sets the second chart's `fig` to the first's title, a field that holds no figure. The plan is that program's:
# the second chart makes a figure of its own, and the screen shows two.

